@mill413/dsh-notify README · @mill413/dsh-notify：English | [中文说明](README.zh.md)

Desktop notifications and configurable HTTP pushes for DeepSeek Harness. Get a reminder when a task stops running or needs approval, an answer, or plan review. Clicking a desktop notification returns you to its session.

The published version is **0.4.2**, validated with npm **DSH 0.2.1-rc.3**. Other host versions have not been verified. MIT licensed.

@mill413/dsh-notify README · HTTP configuration：Requests run on the DSH host. An endpoint containing `localhost` refers to that machine. Supported methods are `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH` and `GET`; GET has no body. You may configure authentication headers, a body template and an icon URL. Endpoint URLs must use HTTP(S) and cannot contain a username or password.

Default body:

```json
{"title":"{{title}}","body":"{{body}}","level":"{{level}}","group":"{{group}}","icon":"{{icon}}"}
```

@mill413/dsh-notify README · Privacy and troubleshooting：- Desktop notifications require HTTPS or a browser-recognized secure local context, browser permission, and an open page. Check system Do Not Disturb and the background-only setting if no alert appears.
- This plugin uses the Notification constructor without a Service Worker. Some mobile browsers do not support it. Use HTTP delivery when the browser will be closed.
- For HTTP failures, verify network reachability, request headers and receiver logs from the host machine, then use **Test push**.
